OL,3,GNEWSAChild obesity rates rise among
OL,4,Ayoungest pupils
OL,5,
OL,6,FLevels of excess weight among young
OL,7,Fchildren in Guernsey are rising, with
OL,8,Fmore than one in five Year 1 pupils now
OL,9,Fclassed as overweight or obese,
OL,10,Faccording to a new report.
OL,12,FThe latest findings from the Guernsey
OL,13,FChild Measurement Programme showed
OL,14,F21.2% of children in Year 1, aged five
OL,15,Fand six, had excess weight in 2026.
OL,16,FAmong Year 5 pupils, aged nine and 10,
OL,17,Fthe figure was 29.7%.
OL,19,FResearchers estimated 294 children
OL,20,Facross the two year groups were living
OL,21,Foverweight or with obesity.
OL,23,APub: 28-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Ch Is NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
